# Settings changed remotely: edit this file in GitHub (or ask Claude to) and the server picks
# it up on its next auto-update (~5 min, with a restart). These win over .env.
# Never put keys or tokens here: anything named *KEY*, *TOKEN*, *SECRET* is ignored.
# Settings changed with /set in Discord win over this file (/settings shows where each comes from).
#
# To make these permanent, follow each change-log entry's action in your server's .env:
#   CHANGE = the setting is already in .env: edit that line (don't add a second copy)
#   ADD    = .env doesn't have it yet: add the line
# then delete it here (or ask Claude to). /envchanges in Discord checks your .env and says which.
#
# ---- Change log (newest first): date · CHANGE/ADD · setting · old → new · why ---------------
# 2026-10-24 · CHANGE · LINEMAKER_SPORTS · NBA,NFL,NHL → NBA,NFL,NHL,MLB · MLB pitcher-change alerts, daily MLB game-line tracking
#
# ---- Active settings (one per line) -------------------------------------------------------
LINEMAKER_SPORTS=NBA,NFL,NHL,MLB
